{"title":"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and circumcenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. A circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are all different and lie on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> in this order. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the points of intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> in this order. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the second point of intersection of the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b93a2dc17d4cf5e91cf1edaa02b2a16f690e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the second point of intersection of the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8640d31c2ebc44d366b103d17cb90aee60baa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CGE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />.<br /><br />\nSuppose that the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d866e6fc173ac133bb53a275bcb17d5212ef25f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FK$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed90c464610d414c09ac1e64786235075641eba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GL$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> are different and intersect at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.<br /><br />\nProposed by Silouanos Brazitikos and Evangelos Psychas, Greece\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><u><b>Lemma</b></u> (On three chords). <i>If two lines pass through different endpoints of two circles' common chord, then the other two chords cut by these lines on the circles are parallel.</i><br />\n<u>Proof</u> The second and the third chords are anti-parallel to the first (common) chord with respect to the given lines, so they are parallel to each other. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12dda010ebddef028cda1ec9d14986f4a26d07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Box$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /><br />\nTo solve this problem, it is sufficient to apply the lemma 5 times. Indeed, let the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d8953473258563eacccdccef4386ab8c5fd2578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD, GE, FK, GL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> second time at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe71277d9598f8128cc1e453da5b5ab9e7f1a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H, I, M, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. One of the circles that figure in lemma is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, while the other is one of three other circles from the problem statement. Applying the lemma to the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a86eacfc54a8fec18a34420dae24876b582ed30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FDH$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/1946d883069b465ce5953376e6a2e1b8a8ab62c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GEI$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/0634d0c302c1844ec6224ad594cbf5c175334a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FKM$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4057c3e63298c2ed6715003afb6f2d9dc6272037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a86eacfc54a8fec18a34420dae24876b582ed30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FDH$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e7d7145909be2e43359b8711a2711b7cd4dfad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BKA$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2eab2dd7bc263e9c9f8e6a5765fc0b9d7c5a017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GLN$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f52863fdb7628708d5fe508796064193c3aa12b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CEB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/1946d883069b465ce5953376e6a2e1b8a8ab62c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GEI$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8a79f6e4af953ccd93b7f7f9c13160ee6ce730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CLA$\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccdcda048c788bd4d96990587ae699bff57bde34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE \\parallel IH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/193c7026c30aed3f1d4dcaf993e899af48206bb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KD \\parallel MC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1baded81823d154d39db13a3ab3dd0bb52cde8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KD \\parallel AH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/720bbb38e7d3db5bc741002ddb850416648c9d0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LE \\parallel NB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ae660615c677b5e5fd300f679f6ae65fd8241a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LE \\parallel AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, respectively. From this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf16c22690c66c9fed08fcd1c8ef904eac9b9087.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC \\parallel IH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd40b3fc57dd5bb149e607436e5cad4d8d4fb386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC \\parallel AH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767c262a0b2b22cb2a03c4dc299113d884565233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NB \\parallel AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e15da09e4399312ba688ca1b653f6724e6b69b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN=IB=HC=AM$\" width=\"190\" height=\"13\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetric wrt <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, a diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. So are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99da1165d799d1ea8e8ce2f4a3fd9219139afc78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF=AG$\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b040068d0a83d6c466d4e893e10967a08f4b25aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25669389bd8875d413eaedb29d7df70cdc95f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GN$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> are symmetric wrt <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and meet on it.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Whilst the logic is exactly the same, I will change the names of the points, so please refer to the following problem statement:\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. A circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> intersects this circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the same side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the same side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. The circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551b922a931c09d035800f66b06b3a9f1ddc5133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BGE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> intersects the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac695ece67ec8ac7e854d2508ffa459d6d067b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K \\neq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />), and the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4058f702f9b49262f62265a4890e14b1bd3c7ff3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CFD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> intersects the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d920be1ef998468e6c76847594440bc9b7f207c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L \\neq C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe8ea79348e2ab934ed8b0812105548fbb6062a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eae1096fc3c1794fdba6e19f5f33e85a8c35b18a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815ad24a9cead8c8d8be115cc3232e6079758226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p>Solution:\n</p><p>To show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, it suffices to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874aeead01d1251f862a042fdc2cce9853e3fc34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XF = XG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is the line through the centers of the two circles, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c585c3b4f4ee632eb660ed60657a90911868290c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KFG = \\angle LGF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4cae83c0fa7a0b33f58a5ec88e27c870c017a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99da1165d799d1ea8e8ce2f4a3fd9219139afc78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF=AG$\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, this is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb30ee517df758b5c3d0afb283ad2ac1abfb22c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFK = \\angle AGL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />. By angle-chasing in the circumcircles, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/494ccdf27abf833db9afac82ec3c5dcd8c5faa81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFK = \\angle AFD - \\angle KFD = 90^\\circ - \\frac{1}{2}\\angle FAD - \\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"441\" height=\"38\" />, and similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129bd2f4f40cc48525d19b9e80d1c64bbba82d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AGL = 90^\\circ - \\frac{1}{2}\\angle GAE - \\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"273\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, we must show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc973d269f94d8115f973b1ca5c6b7ac31a82f1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\angle FAD + \\angle ABC = \\frac{1}{2}\\angle GAE + \\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"319\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c7846952e7b2c0dc7e48efe920bc67379336d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FAD - \\angle GAE = 2(\\angle ACB - \\angle ABC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"20\" />. Expanding the angles gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1dec70297402a1eda12ac523ed95d46f0783ebc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\angle FAB - \\angle GAC) + (\\angle BAD - \\angle CAE) = 2(\\angle ACB - \\angle ABC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"500\" height=\"20\" />. Using the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/97810909f25bd6d360ff09d294fb9013fbb2cb84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD - \\angle CAE = \\angle ADE - \\angle ABD - (\\angle AED - \\angle ACE) = \\angle ACB - \\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"623\" height=\"20\" />, the equation reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c57db8c6f8f2c2b342d7894f5391adb3a480421a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FAB - \\angle GAC = \\angle ACB - \\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"292\" height=\"16\" />. Noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8f1ffc62ade78534e55bc4e146c66758e4447d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB - \\angle FAB = \\angle ACF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d2778b664ec5fb2b6af6643cb25cfd10f54125aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC - \\angle GAC = \\angle ABG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"16\" />, the condition becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6ca86a8df1386871583745f2f6c8fdf742241d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABG = \\angle ACF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />, which corresponds to arcs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f068f0bf681b3a7ba788899bf7748542cb35036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\stackrel{\\frown}{AG} = \\stackrel{\\frown}{AF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"24\" />, which clearly holds true as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the circle passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>-yang71\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO\" title=\"2015 IMO\">2015 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000531\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 639/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20438/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.358      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.358      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14370:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018000531 and revision id 281244. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}